>> To ensure that Nethack conforms to the legislation that seems likely
>> to be passed in Britain (except Scotland where similar legislation
>> already applies), I've written a small patch to dissuade Nethack
>> players from using dogs to hunt foxes. I would encourage players in
>> Scotland to apply it immediately, and all other British-based players
>> to apply it before the legislation comes into force.
> 
> Heh, nice one. Just for the source-illiterate among us, what exactly
> does it do? 
> 

When your dog kills a fox it checks to see whether any humanoid can see 
both you and the dog (and is awake etc.). If there is a humanoid it summons 
the Kops.

Notes:

It must be a dog, there are no laws (proposed or otherwise) against hunting 
foxes with cats or Archons.

'Humanoid' covers things like kobolds, nymphs & bugbears as well as humans. 
Zombies are specifically excluded (maybe they are hunt supporters?)

For a low level character the best action to take when you see your dog 
heading for a fox is probably to run away as fast as you can. So long as 
you get out of sight you should be alright.

I think it's nice giving the Kops an extra role: I only use Kop-safe 
methods of stealing from shops, so I don't normally ever see them.

